WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.362
Day two is run by the people who touch
the estate most and decide the least,

2
00:00:04.362 --> 00:00:08.962
so the design puts every decision with
someone who isn't holding the keyboard.

3
00:00:08.962 --> 00:00:11.087
The slide shows one decider per row,

4
00:00:11.087 --> 00:00:15.334
from the CISO's verification procedure
to the change advisory board,

5
00:00:15.334 --> 00:00:19.288
which authorizes changes even to
the approval rules themselves.

6
00:00:19.288 --> 00:00:22.775
Only the authorizing official
accepts open-ended risk.

7
00:00:22.775 --> 00:00:25.076
The separations on the
right are the ones the

8
00:00:25.076 --> 00:00:27.812
platform should enforce
rather than leave to memory.

9
00:00:27.812 --> 00:00:30.368
Above all, nobody approves their own work,

10
00:00:30.368 --> 00:00:33.224
and nobody changes the
gate they pass through.

11
00:00:33.224 --> 00:00:36.580
Contractors can prepare every
decision here except the

12
00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:39.863
authorizing official's, which
is a government-only role.

13
00:00:39.863 --> 00:00:41.620
So, what to decide first?
